{
  "_about": [
    "Golden cases for reading the account store as all or nothing: which records a read is missing.",
    "Normative: docs/account-store.md §A complete answer.",
    "Each case gives the manifest's ids (`manifest_ids`), the ids whose returned value opened under its own id (`returned`), the ids whose returned value did not open (`unreadable`, default empty) and the ids the reader already holds, decoded, from an earlier read (`held`). An id the reader holds but could not decode is not held. A returned id the manifest does not list is ignored.",
    "`missing` is, in the manifest's order, every listed id that did not come back opened and is not held, plus every listed id whose value came back unreadable even when it is held. A value that does not open (random bytes, another id's value, a version byte the reader does not know) is never another build's record: every writer seals version 0x01. The reader keeps a held copy as it was meanwhile.",
    "A reader with anything missing asks once more for exactly those ids. `again`, when present, is that second answer (`returned`, `unreadable`), and `refused` says whether the read is then refused: every id asked for again must come back and open, and the version must not have moved. A refused read keeps the reader's cached store, version and floor.",
    "To replay: run each case through your own implementation of the format and compare the result with the case's expectation, field by field."
  ],
